      "problem": "What picture is missing from the multiplication model below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130082/assets/39c8668bd4bf5309b708769a99d9d3fa2184f0937411d437de8a1195853e5118.png)",
      "worked_solution": "In the model, we have $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ on the left.\n\nSince we are multiplying by $\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}5}$, we need to split the whole into $\\color{blue}5$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130082/assets/6584c694fbbc990dfa3b58a19545d3deb9889f162da6e02a9820310a190ae04e.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\dfrac{1}{20}$ of the whole.\n\nThe missing picture is:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130082/assets/e349233ebb5e3927f0d4bda98cb2470c1f17574a522d2f4b9cbddaf365fe946d.png)",
